{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good picture of the media library:\n- Logo (4:8, 96×96)\n- Avatar_Neutral (4:11, 96×96)\n- Gen_Mug (4:19, 200×200), Gen_Rat (4:22, 133×200), Gen_Statue (4:25, 300×200), Gen_Student (4:28, 281×200)\n- PDF_File_Icon (4:31, 64×64)\n- Logo_Google (4:42, 48×48), Logo_Facebook (4:48, 48×48)\n- Icons: Icon_Email, Icon_Password, Icon_Show, Icon_Plus, Icon_Search, Icon_Chats, Icon_Archive, Icon_Image, Icon_Document_PDF, Icon_Back, Icon_Arrow_Up_Right, Icon_Edit, Icon_Copy, Icon_Share, Icon_Regenerate, Icon_Download, Icon_Send, Icon_Menu, Icon_Export, Icon_Close, Icon_Premium, Icon_More, Icon_Delete\n- Story_Text (4:203)\n\nNow I need to get design context for key nodes to understand the exact appearance of the components (Button, Text Field, Status Bar, Home Indicator) and the media (Logo, Avatar, images, icons). Let me use use_figma read-only calls to inspect and also to copy assets.\n\nActually, an efficient approach: use use_figma with plugin API code to:\n1. First inspect node structures (get design context) for components like Button (3:24), Text Field (3:29), Status Bar (3:34), Home Indicator (3:45), Logo (4:8), Avatar (4:11), and Story_Text content (4:203).\n\nThe metadata tool says I should call get_design_context for implementation. But I have the use_figma tool which can do everything. Let me use use_figma read-only to inspect and get text contents.\n\nLet me first check the Story_Text content and the components' internals via use_figma.\n\nPlan for the build:\n\nDesign system (my decisions):\n- Colors:\n  - Primary: #612A74\n  - Primary pressed/dark: #4E2260\n  - Background: #FFFFFF or #F7F5F9\n  - Surface: #FFFFFF\n  - Surface secondary: #F5F2F7 (light lavender gray)\n  - Text primary: #1A1523 (near black)\n  - Text secondary: #6E6478 (gray)\n  - Text tertiary/disabled: #A79FB0\n  - Border: #E4DFEA\n  - Success: #1F9D55\n  - Warning: #B45309 / #D97706\n  - Error/destructive: #DC2626\n  - Storage colors: Chats #612A74, Images #9B5FB0 (lighter purple), Exports #C9A6D6 or teal? Let me pick: Chats #612A74 (primary purple), Images #A05BC4 (mid purple), Exports #D9BFE8 (light purple). Actually better differentiation: Chats #612A74, Images #9B6BC7, Exports #CBA8DE. Hmm, or use distinct hues: Chats purple #612A74, Images magenta/pink #A64AC9, Exports lavender #D0B3E0. That works within brand.\n\n- Type scale (Nunito for body, Bricolage Grotesque for display/headers):\n  - Large title: Bricolage Grotesque 28/SemiBold (login title)\n  - Title: Bricolage Grotesque 22 SemiBold (screen titles)\n  - Header: Bricolage Grotesque 20 SemiBold\n  - Body: Nunito 15 Regular\n  - Body medium: Nunito 15 SemiBold\n  - Caption: Nunito 13\n  - Small: Nunito 12\n  - Button: Nunito 17 SemiBold (fixed)\n\n- Spacing: 4/8/12/16/20/24\n- Radii: 16 (cards), 12 (small), 24-28 (sheets), full (buttons/pills)\n- Elevation: subtle shadows.\n\nScreens (12 frames, 428×928):\n1. 01_Login — logo, \"Login to your account\", email field filled \"sam.rivera@example.com\", password field masked \"••••••••\" with show/hide icon, Login button, \"Or login with\" Facebook/Google, \"Don't have an account? Sign Up\", Terms of use | Privacy policy. → Login button → 02_Home_Chats\n2. 02_Home_Chats — header: back icon, avatar, \"Start a new chat with Chat Bot AI\" + logo, New Topic button, History title + search field, view switcher (Chats/Archived/Images/Exports, Chats selected), 7 chat rows with question (bold), answer preview (2 lines ellipsized), time; chat 2 shows Gen_Student image. Links: New Topic → 05, chat (the story chat) → 06, Images tab → 03, Exports tab → 04, avatar → 08.\n3. 03_Home_Images — same header, switcher Images selected, grid of 8 images: Gen_Mug, Gen_Rat, Gen_Statue, Gen_Student, Gen_Statue, Gen_Mug, Gen_Rat, Gen_Student. Links: Chats → 02, Exports → 04, New Topic → 05.\n4. 04_Home_Exports — same header, switcher Exports, 7 PDF rows with PDF icon, title, date, size. Links: Chats → 02, Images → 03, New Topic → 05.\n5. 05_Chat_New — header: menu, export icons? \"Actions: menu · export · send\". Assistant: logo + \"Chat Bot AI 4.5\" + \"Premium account\" (with premium icon). \"How can I help you my friend? 😊\". Input empty \"Ask me anything...\", send button. 4 suggestion cards (Brainstorm names / Suggest some codenames / Write a SQL query / Explain why popcorn pops). Link: menu → 02.\n6. 06_Chat_Conversation — same header (menu, export), conversation: You (bubble right, primary color), Chat Bot AI (bubble left with logo avatar?). 4 messages: You story question; AI story text (long, truncated at frame end but full text is on media); You image description; AI \"I'll try to create that...\" + Gen_Student image. Message actions: on You messages Edit · Copy; on story Copy · Share · Regenerate; on image Download · Share · Regenerate. Link: menu → 02, export → 07 (07 shows sheet over 06).\n7. 07_Export_PDF_Sheet — sheet over 06: dimmed background + bottom sheet with close, PDF_File_Icon, \"Export as PDF\", copy text, Title field \"The story of a student\", Export button. Links: close → 06, Export → 06.\n8. 08_Profile_Settings — back, more, avatar, Sam Rivera, premium account, 278 days, \"Profile & Settings\", settings list: Email sam.rivera@example.com, Change password, Theme \"System default\" (→10), Data & storage \"83% Used\" (→11), Send feedback with note. Footer: \"Chat Bot AI - Version 2.0.5\", Terms of use, Privacy policy. Links: back → 02, more → 09, Theme → 10, Data & storage → 11.\n9. 09_Account_Actions_Sheet — sheet over 08: dim, \"Delete Account\" (destructive), \"Sign out\". Links: Sign out → 01, tap outside → 08.\n10. 10_Theme_Sheet — sheet over 08: options Dark mode / Light mode / System default (selected, radio), tap outside → 08.\n11. 11_Cloud_Space — back, more, \"Cloud Space\", storage usage \"12.48 GB of 15 GB used\" with segmented bar (Chats 25%, Images 55%, Exports 3%), sections: Images (169 Item, 8,225 MB, note, 7 thumbnails), Exports (37 Item, 506 MB, note, 3 rows with delete), Clear cache (238.05 MB) → 12, Delete all chats (12.48 GB) with warning. Footer same as 08. Links: back → 08, Clear cache → 12.\n12. 12_Clear_Cache_Dialog — dialog over 11: \"Clear cache\", copy, Cancel / Delete buttons. Links: Cancel → 11, Delete → 11.\n\nTotal 12 frames. Prototype links as listed.\n\nFor sheets (07, 09, 10) and dialog (12), the brief says \"sheet over 06_Chat_Conversation; the conversation stays behind it\" — meaning the frame includes the parent screen dimmed behind. So frames 07, 09, 10, 12 will be 428×928 frames containing a copy of the parent screen (dimmed) + sheet/dialog overlay. That's the standard approach for these benchmarks.\n\nApproach to build:\n1. First inspect components in detail via use_figma (read-only): Button (3:24), Text Field (3:29), Status Bar (3:34), Home Indicator (3:45) internals — to replicate styles. Also read Story_Text (4:203) full text, and get fills of the gen images.\n2. Build components in 03 · Workspace:\n   - Platform shell instances (use the actual component instances from 02? The instruction says \"Reuse the components in 02 · Components\" — I can create instances of Status Bar / Home Indicator / Button / Text Field directly in the workspace. Since they're in the same file, instances work across pages.)\n   - My own components: Header for home, view switcher, chat list item, image grid tile, export row, message bubbles (user/AI), message action row, suggestion card, settings row, sheet container, dialog, storage bar, etc.\n\nSimpler robust approach: Since the plugin API with instances of the given components is doable, but building via component components adds complexity. The evaluation criteria mention \"Component reuse\" — I should create reusable components for business components. But time/token constraints matter. A pragmatic approach: create components for key repeated items (chat row, export row, image tile, message bubbles, settings row, s