f fonts) {\n  if ([\"Bricolage Grotesque\",\"Nunito\",\"Inter\"].includes(f.fontName.family)) {\n    fams[f.fontName.family] = fams[f.fontName.family] || [];\n    fams[f.fontName.family].push(f.fontName.style);\n  }\n}\nout.fonts = fams;\n\nfunction dump(n, d) {\n  const o = { id: n.id, name: n.name, type: n.type, w: n.width, h: n.height, x: n.x, y: n.y };\n  if (\"fills\" in n) o.fills = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(n.fills));\n  if (\"strokes\" in n) o.strokes = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(n.strokes));\n  if (\"strokeWeight\" in n) o.strokeWeight = n.strokeWeight;\n  if (\"cornerRadius\" in n) o.radius = n.cornerRadius;\n  if (n.type === \"TEXT\") { o.chars = n.characters; o.font = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(n.fontName)); o.fontSize = n.fontSize; }\n  if (n.type === \"COMPONENT\") o.isComponent = true;\n  if (d > 0 && \"children\" in n) o.children = n.children.map(c => dump(c, d-1));\n  return o;\n}\nconst ids = [\"3:24\",\"3:29\",\"3:34\",\"3:45\",\"4:8\",\"4:11\",\"4:19\",\"4:22\",\"4:25\",\"4:28\",\"4:31\",\"4:42\",\"4:48\",\"4:203\",\"4:58\",\"4:76\",\"4:164\",\"4:189\",\"4:197\"];\nout.nodes = ids.map(id => { const n = figma.getNodeById(id); return n ? dump(n, 2) : { id, missing: true }; });\nreturn JSON.stringify(out).slice(0, 49000);\n```\n\nWait — use_figma returns what the code returns? The tool presumably returns console output / return value. Let me keep output under limit. Also `figma.getNodeById` is deprecated in favor of `await figma.getNodeByIdAsync`. I'll use getNodeByIdAsync.\n\nFont size: fontSize could be figma.mixed for mixed text; JSON stringify of mixed... I'll guard with try.\n\nLet me also check the Text Field's placeholder and Button label characters.\n\nThen build. Let me now also think about what the Story_Text contains — I'll get its characters (462px tall, width 1472 — likely ~1500 chars). I'll take the first portion for the truncated display. Since I control display, I'll set the story bubble text to the first ~45 words + \"…\". Actually to