e → 11.\n\nComponents to create (in a components area on workspace page):\n- MyButton/Secondary (ghost, primary text, border) — for Cancel, social buttons variant? Social: outline w/ logo+label — one-off.\n- MyButton/Destructive — filled red \"Delete\".\n- ViewSwitcher with variants (Chats/Images/Exports selected) — or single component with 4 tabs and I override per-instance fills of the selected pill... Overriding per-instance fill of one pill + its text is doable but fiddly. Variants cleaner: component set \"ViewSwitcher\" with 3 variants used (Archived view never shown as selected since no screen). Actually Archived never current → only 3 variants.\n- ChatListItem component (with thumb variant?) — I'll make base row + separate variant with image thumb. Or just build row 2 ad-hoc. To show component reuse, make ChatListItem (variants: Default / WithImage).\n- ExportRow component.\n- ImageTile component (square with image fill) — instances override fill.\n- MessageBubble/User, MessageBubble/AI (variants: Text / WithImage? AI story vs AI image differ: story = text only + actions; image = text + image + actions). I'll make AI bubble component with everything and override visibility? Simpler: two components.\n- MessageActions component? Actions differ (Edit+Copy for user; Copy+Share+Regenerate for story; Download+Share+Regenerate for image). Make MessageActions a component with the 3-action row and hide/show first item per instance? Overriding visibility of instance children is allowed. For user messages: Edit+Copy (2 items). Story: Copy+Share+Regenerate. Image: Download+Share+Regenerate. Hmm labels differ in first slot. Easier: hand-build each actions row inline (they're small), skip componentization here. But \"Component reuse\" evaluation — I'll have plenty of reused components already. For pragmatism: build actions as components with 3 slots and override icon+label per instance? Icon override = swap fills — icons are component instances themselves; swapping which i