sitions... Actually there IS: TransitionInstant? I don't recall. Safest: omit the field.\n\nAlso flow starting points: try page.flowStartingPoints = frames.map(f => ({nodeId: f.id, name: f.name})). Writable? I believe PageNode.flowStartingPoints is read-only... Let me check: In plugin docs, `flowStartingPoints: ReadonlyArray<FlowStartingPoint>` on PageNode — read-only. Hmm. But there's `figma.root`... Prototype flows are usually created in UI. The tool benchmark says \"wire them as a clickable prototype\" — connections (reactions) are the key part. Flow starting points default to first frame? In prototype view, any frame without incoming connections can serve as a start. Not critical. I'll try setting it; if throws, catch and continue.\n\nHmm wait — actually I recall the REST API / plugin dev: `figma.currentPage.flowStartingPoints` — docs show it under PageNode as writable? \"flowStartingPoints: ReadonlyArray<FlowStartingPoint>\" — the ReadonlyArray means the array itself is readonly but... it's a get-only property. I'll attempt assignment in try/catch.\n\nReactions writability: I'm fairly confident node.reactions is writable in plugin API (docs: \"reactions: ReadonlyArray<Reaction>\" — hmm also ReadonlyArray). Damn. If reactions is read-only, I cannot wire prototypes via plugin API?! \n\nLet me think harder. Figma Plugin API documentation: there IS `Reaction` type and `node.reactions` — I remember community threads: \"Creating prototype connections via plugin API\" — historically NOT possible; reactions was read-only. Then in 2023 Figma shipped `figma.on(\"prototypeloader\")`? no... \n\nActually — I now recall clearly: Figma announced Plugin API support for prototype connections in 2023: the `reactions` property became WRITABLE. Announcement: \"Prototype interactions in the Plugin API\" — yes, July 2023 \"You can now create and edit prototype connections using the Plugin API\" — the API: `node.reactions = [{trigger, action}]`. Types: ReactionTrigger {type: \"CLICK\"|\"MOUSE_ENTER\"|\"MOUSE_LEAVE\"|\"MOUSE_PRESS\"|\"MOUSE_RELEASE\"|\"DRAG\"|\"KEYBOARD\"|\"AFTER_TIMEOUT\"|\"MOUSE_HOVER\"}, ReactionAction {type:\"BACK\"|\"NODE\"|\"URL\"|\"CLOSE\"}, ReactionActionNode {type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\"|\"SWAP\"|\"OVERLAY\"|\"SCROLL_TO\"|\"CHANGE_TO\", transition, preserveState, resetScrollPosition, overlay...}. Yes — writable. I'm going with it, in try/catch with console output for verification.\n\nOne more consideration: the clone-based \"sheet over parent\" frames (07/09/10/12): cloning 06 into 07 means 07 contains a copy incl. status bar etc. The dim overlay covers it. Good. But watch out: cloned frame inside a frame — nested frame size 428×928 at 0,0. Fine.\n\nAlso links FROM 06's export button → 07; close in 07 → 06; export in 07 → 06.\n\nEdge: 07 clone will contain reactions pointing to 02/05 etc. (menu → 02). Those remain on the dimmed copy — clickable behind dim? The dim rect would cover them (hotspots under a rect still trigger? In Figma prototype, topmost node with reaction receives click; the dim rect has no reaction → click passes to... actually nodes without reactions don't capture; the click may hit the clone's nodes beneath. To avoid weirdness, put a transparent hotspot rect covering whole frame ABOVE dim but BELOW sheet, with reaction → 06? That would make entire background tap → 06 (acts as tap-outside). Not listed for 07 but harmless and sensible. Hmm \"Do not add frames beyond the 12\" refers to frames; extra hotspot fine. I'll add tap-outside hotspot → 06 for 07 too. Wait actually for 07 I said skip extra links; but a background hotspot preventing weird clicks is protective. I'll add it (→ 06). Fine.\n\nFor 09/10: listed \"tap outside → 08\" — add hotspot over dim area → 08. For 12: links only Cancel/Delete → 11; I'll add background hotspot → 11 as well for safety.\n\nAlso dim rect itself: make hotspot = the dim rect (fill black 45% + reaction). Simple.\n\nStatus bar instance on cloned frames: clone includes it — fine.\n\nNow, what about \"04 · Media\" Story_Text: I need its actual first words for the story bubble. Get in inspection.\n\nLet me also dump fills of Gen_ images to get imageHash. ImageHash appears in fill as imageHash property. \n\nAlso Avatar_Neutral hash. And Logo — instance directly.\n\nPDF icon, premium icon — instances.\n\nLet me write inspection code now. Also verify the components' property definitions:\n\n```\nconst btn = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"3:24\");\nout.btnProps = btn.componentPropertyDefinitions;\n```\n\nAlso check 3:29.\n\nAlso I want the exact visual style of given Button/Text Field to align my own components: dump depth 3.\n\nLet me also read 4:203 characters (full story). Could be ~2500 chars — include as-is (need it for truncated story text; I'll craft bubble text from its beginning).\n\nAlso — important — check page 5:2 (03 · Workspace) current contents: metadata said empty? It listed nothing under 5:2 earlier (get_metadata of 5:2 wasn't called). Let me include in inspection: dump children of page 5:2.\n\nAlright, let me also confirm: use_figma code param max 50000 chars. My return values should be modest.\n\nOne more: the icon components might have internal structure with fills I want to match text colors. I'll recolor per use.\n\nInspection call:\n\n```js\nconst out = {};\nasync function g(id){ return await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id); }\nconst fonts = await figma.listAvailableFontsAsync();\nconst fams = {};\nfor (const f of fonts) {\n  const fam = f.fontName.family;\n  if (fam === \"Bricolage Grotesque\" || fam === \"Nunito\") {\n    (fams[fam] = fams[fam] || []).push(f.fontName.style);\n  }\n}\nout.fonts = fams;\n\nfunction dump(n, d) {\n  const o = { t: n.type, n: n.name, id: n.id, w: Math.round(n.width*10)/10, h: Math.round(n.height*10)/10 };\n  try { if (\"fills\" in n && n.fills !== figma.mixed) o.f = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(n.fills)); } catch(e){}\n  try { if (\"strokes\" in n && n.strokes !== figma.m