e 11.5/16 sub 2-3 lines; thumbnails row: 7 × 48 (radius 10) gap 6 → 7×48+6×6=372 ≤ 352? card inner width 380-28=352 < 372. Use 44: 7×44+36=344 ✓. Card height ~ 14+22+8+48(3-line note?) note ~2 lines 32 + 10 + 44 + 14 ≈ 144.\n- Exports card: header row similar (\"Exports\" + \"37 Item\" + \"506 MB\"); note 2 lines; 3 rows: title 13 SemiBold trunc1 + meta \"DEC 30, 2023 · 2.16 MB\" 11.5 sub + Icon_Delete 16 danger right; row h 44 ×3 + dividers. Card ~ 14+22+8+32+10+3×46 ≈ 226.\n- Clear cache card row: Icon_Delete? label \"Clear cache\" + value \"238.05 MB\" + chevron; h 56. → 12\n- Delete all chats card: row: \"Delete all chats\" (danger SemiBold 15) + \"12.48 GB\" 13 sub + chevron; warning text below in card (11.5/16 warn, 2-3 lines). h ~ 96.\n- Footer: version + links.\nTotal: 95+120+10+144+10+226+10+56+8+96+10+footer 50 ≈ 835 ✓ fits under 894? 47+... let me sum from y=47: header 44 (51→95), storage 95..215, images 225..369, exports 379..605, clear 615..671, delete 679..775, footer 790..846. ✓\n\n12 dialog: clone 11 → dim → dialog 320 wide centered y≈370, h≈230: title \"Clear cache\" Bricolage SemiBold 20 center; copy 13/18 sub center width 264; buttons row: Cancel (secondary: bg fieldBg? design: bg #F2EEF5 text dark 15 SemiBold, radius 24, h 48, w 144) + Delete (bg danger, white). Links Cancel→11, Delete→11, dim→11.\n\n09 sheet: clone 08 → dim → sheet y=688? height 240: grabber; row \"Sign out\" (Icon_Arrow_Up_Right 20 + text 16 SemiBold dark) h 60 → 01; divider; row \"Delete Account\" (Icon_Delete 20 danger + text danger) → no link. Links: Sign out→01, dim→08. \"tap outside → 08\" ✓.\n\n10 sheet: clone 08 → dim → sheet y=568 h 360: grabber + title \"Theme\" Bricolage 20 + 3 option rows h 56: radio circle 22 (border 2; selected: fill primary + inner white dot) + label 15; \"System default\" selected. Options order: Dark mode, Light mode, System default (current). Links: dim→08.\n\nPrototype wiring summary (after all frames):\n- 01: Login button → 02\n- 02: NewTopic → 05; story chat card → 06; Images tab → 03; Exports tab → 04; avatar → 08\n- 03: Chats tab → 02; Exports tab → 04; NewTopic → 05\n- 04: Chats tab → 02; Images tab → 03; NewTopic → 05\n- 05: menu icon → 02\n- 06: menu → 02; export → 07\n- 07: close → 06; Export → 06; dim → 06\n- 08: back → 02; more → 09; Theme row → 10; Data & storage row → 11\n- 09: Sign out → 01; dim → 08\n- 10: dim → 08\n- 11: back → 08; Clear cache card → 12\n- 12: Cancel → 11; Delete → 11; dim → 11\n\nAlso flow starting points: try page.flowStartingPoints = all 12.\n\nNow Call 2: components. Let me write the code.\n\nKey helpers (repeat in each call):\n\n```js\nconst PAGE = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"5:2\");\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(PAGE);\nconst BR = (s)=>({family:\"Bricolage Grotesque\",style:s});\nconst NU = (s)=>({family:\"Nunito\",style:s});\nawait Promise.all([\n  figma.loadFontAsync(BR(\"Regular\")),figma.loadFontAsync(BR(\"Medium\")),figma.loadFontAsync(BR(\"SemiBold\")),figma.loadFontAsync(BR(\"Bold\")),\n  figma.loadFontAsync(NU(\"Regular\")),figma.loadFontAsync(NU(\"Medium\")),figma.loadFontAsync(NU(\"SemiBold\")),figma.loadFontAsync(NU(\"Bold\")),figma.loadFontAsync(NU(\"ExtraBold\"))\n]);\nconst HEX={primary:\"612A74\",primaryDark:\"4A2160\",tint:\"F5EEF8\",bg:\"F7F5F9\",surface:\"FFFFFF\",text:\"211A2B\",sub:\"6B6176\",faint:\"A79DB2\",border:\"E7E2EC\",field:\"F2EEF5\",danger:\"D93843\",warn:\"C77700\",ok:\"2E9E5B\",stChats:\"612A74\",stImg:\"9E5FC1\",stExp:\"D9C1E8\",stFree:\"ECE6F0\"};\nconst hx=h=>({r:parseInt(h.slice(0,2),16)/255,g:parseInt(h.slice(2,4),16)/255,b:parseInt(h.slice(4,6),16)/255});\nconst S=(h,o)=>{const p={type:\"SOLID\",color:hx(h)};if(o!=null)p.opacity=o;return p;};\nfunction T(chars,font,size,color,o={}){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName=font;t.fontSize=size;t.characters=chars;t.fills=[S(color,o.op)];if(o.lh)t.lineHeight={value:o.lh,unit:\"PIXELS\"};if(o.ls)t.letterSpacing={value:o.ls,unit:\"PERCENT\"};t.name=o.name||chars.slice(0,24).replace(/\\n/g,\" \");return t;}\nfunction fit(t,w,maxLines){t.resize(w,t.height);t.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\";if(maxLines){t.textTruncation=\"ENDING\";t.maxLines=maxLines;}return t;}\nfunction F(name,w,h,fill,r){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;f.resize(w,h);f.fills=fill?[Array.isArray(fill)?fill[0]:fill]:[];if(r)f.cornerRadius=r;return f;}\n```\n\nHmm fills param messy; I'll write two helpers: F (plain frame, fill hex or null) and stack helpers:\n\n```js\nfunction V(name,w,gap,fill,pad,r){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;f.layoutMode=\"VERTICAL\";f.itemSpacing=gap;f.fills=fill?[S(fill)]:[];if(r)f.cornerRadius=r;if(pad){f.paddingTop=pad[0];f.paddingRight=pad[1];f.paddingBottom=pad[2];f.paddingLeft=pad[3];}f.resize(w,10);f.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";f.counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";return f;}\nfunction H(name,h,gap,fill,pad,r){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;f.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\";f.itemSpacing=gap;f.counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";f.fills=fill?[S(fill)]:[];if(r)f.cornerRadius=r;if(pad){f.paddingTop=pad[0];f.paddingRight=pad[1];f.paddingBottom=pad[2];f.paddingLeft=pad[3];}f.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";f.counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";f.resize(10,h);return f;}\n```\nNote: for auto layout frames, set resize after? With primaryAxisSizingMode AUTO the primary dimension hugs; counter FIXED uses resize value. For V: width fixed = counter axis → counterAxisSizingMode FIXED with resize(w,10) sets width w. For H: height fixed = counter axis. Good.\n\nFill-width children: child.layoutSizingHorizontal=\"FILL\" (for text in V stack) / \"FILL\" in H stacks.\n\nIcon helper:\n```js\nconst ICON_IDS={email:\"4:58\",password:\"4:64\",show:\"4:70\",plus:\"4:76\",search:\"4:82\",chats:\"4:87\",archive:\"4:94\",image:\"4:101\",pdf:\"4:110\",back:\"4:116\",arrow:\"4:121\",edit:\"4:128\",copy:\"4:134\",share:\"4:139\",regen:\"4:145\",download:\"4:152\",send:\"4:157\",menu:\"4:164\",export:\"4:171\",close:\"4:177\",premium:\"4:182\",more:\"4:189\",del:\"4:197\"};\nconst ICON_COMP={}; for(const k in ICON_IDS){ICON_COMP[k]=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(ICON_IDS[k]);}\nfunction IC(kind,size,color){const inst=ICON_COMP[kind].createInstance();const sc=size/inst.width;inst.rescale(sc);if(color){for(const c of inst.findAll(n=>n.type===\"VECTOR\")){if(Array.isArray(c.strokes)&&c.strokes.length)c.strokes=[S(color)];if(Array.isArray(c.fills)&&c.fills.length&&c.fills[0].type===\"SOLID\")c.fills=[S(color)];}}inst.name=\"icon/\"+kind;return inst;}\n```\nCareful: Google/Facebook logos multi-color — don't recolor those (not in IC list; separate helper G_LOGO without recolor).\n\nAlso image rects:\n```js\nconst IMGS={mug:\"b33e106bff3f641b1402654e9d9d5ffdf2a99637\",rat:\"69eb0235ba6c4ae0e2fade7e7cf9ee08b2857f0f\",statue:\"d6fed4696134f62100e5e107b55526d302491cde\",student:\"13287f16160feaa047f4e410175f8eea38c72198\",pdf:\"ec7a1e4bdcb78b49dae4e3467913fb50db21088a\",logo:\"f8f9b5b3858b794701361638e2a43a34013ec18c\"};\nfunction IMG(kind,w,h,r){const rc=figma.createRectangle();rc.resize(w,h);if(r)rc.cornerRadius=r;rc.fills=[{type:\"IMAGE\",scaleMode:\"FILL\",imageHash:IMGS[kind]}];rc.name=\"img/\"+kind;return rc;}\n```\nFor logo — the Logo component is just a rect with image fill; using IMG('logo') is equivalent and simpler. But instruction says \"Use the logo ... from 04 · Media\" — using its image fill IS using the media. Also I could instance the Logo component. For sizes, IMG is easier. I'll mostly use IMG with hashes (they come from the media nodes). For avatar — Avatar_Neutral is vector shapes (not image) → use component instance resized via rescale.\n\nAvatar helper:\n```js\nconst AV=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"4:11\"));\nfunction AVAT(size){const inst=AV.createInstance();inst.rescale(size/96);inst.name=\"avatar\";return inst;}\n```\n\nStatus bar & home indicator:\n```js\nconst SB=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"3:34\"); const HI=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"3:45\");\nfunction shell(fr){const a=SB.createInstance();fr.appendChild(a);a.x=0;a.y=0;const b=HI.createInstance();fr.appendChild(b);b.x=0;b.y=894;}\n```\nStatus bar has white fill bg — on login (white bg) fine; on app bg #F7F5F9 slight mismatch. Override instance fill to bg color? Instance root fill override allowed: a.fills=[S(HEX.bg)]. I'll do per screen.\n\nGiven Button & TextField:\n```js\nconst BTN=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"3:24\"); const TF=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"3:29\");\nfunction bigBtn(label){const i=BTN.createInstance();i.setProperties({\"Label#3:0\":label});return i;}\nfunction field(placeholder){const i=TF.createInstance();i.setProperties({\"Placeholder#3:1\":placeholder});return i;}\n```\nWait — for Button used on screens with bg #F7F5F9 the white? Button bg is primary — fine.\n\nNow Components call 2. Components to create (all appended to PAGE, positioned in components zone y=3300+, x spacing):\n\n1. `SW / ViewSwitcher` set with variants. Build one switcher builder function param selected: container H auto layout? I want fixed 380 width: V stack? Single H stack w=380 h=36 padding 4 gap 4 bg #EFE9F3 radius 12; 4 pills each: H hug padding h:12 v:6? pill: H frame padding 12/6 radius 9 bg (primary if selected else transparent) children: icon? Tabs with icons? Keep text-only pills (Nunito SemiBold 13). Pills hug → container fixed width 380: children spacing uneven; set primaryAxisAlignItems=\"SPACE_BETWEEN\"? With hug pills + space-between, looks fine. Hmm but 4 pills hug total width < 372 → space-between distributes. Selected pill wider (padding same, text differs) — acceptable.\n   Tab labels: Chats, Archived, Images, Exports.\n   Selected color: bg primary, text white. Unselected: text sub.\n   Variant property: after building 3 switchers (sel=Chats/Images/Exports), combineAsVariants([a,b,c], PAGE) → set name \"ViewSwitcher\", variants named \"View=Chats\" etc via child.name = \"View=Chats\".\n2. `List / Chat Item` variants: Default & WithImage.\n   Default: V card w=380, pad 12/14, gap 4, bg surface, radius 16