tAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\" keeps width fixed. For short text bubble looks wide. Alternative: measure: after setting chars, if t.width>280: t.resize(280,h); autoResize HEIGHT; else leave WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT. I'll do that logic per instance in build calls.\n   Component: bubble with default text \"Message text\" (hug).\n8. `Chat / Bubble AI`: same but bg surface stroke border, text color text. Default text \"Message text\".\n9. `Chat / Message Actions`: H gap 18: 3 items: H gap 5: icon inst (copy 14 sub) + T(12 Medium sub). item names \"act1\",\"act2\",\"act3\" with icon child name \"a1i\" etc. Per instance: set labels, swap icons via findOne(...).swapComponent.\n10. `New / Input Bar`? one-off per screen (05,06) — hand-build.\n11. `Settings / Premium Badge`: H hug pad 10/5 gap 5 bg tint radius 12: IC premium 13 primary + T(\"premium account\" 12 SemiBold primary). Used 08. Could also be used in 06 header assistant. Yes reuse!\n\nAlso `Header / Home` (used 3×): V w 428 pad 8/24 gap 10 fill none:\n  r1: H FILL h 24: IC back 22 text; spacer (FILL); AVAT 36 — heights differ (24 vs 36): counterAxisAlignItems \"MIN\"? avatar 36, back 22 aligned center. Set r1 counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\", h 36.\n  r2: H FILL gap 10: IMG logo 34; title T(\"Start a new chat with Chat Bot AI\", BR SemiBold 21, text) — one line; FILL trunc 1.\n  r3: H FILL gap 10: NewTopic pill (H hug pad 14/9 gap 6 bg primary r19: IC plus 15 white + T(\"New Topic\", NU SemiBold 14, white)); search (H FILL h 40 pad 12 gap 8 bg field r20: IC search 17 sub; T(\"Search ...\", NU Regular 14, faint)).\n  r4: T(\"History\", NU Bold 16, text).\n  Height ≈ 8+36+10+36+10+40+10+22+8 = 180. Hmm slightly more than planned 156; list start y = 47+180+12 = 239. List budget = 894-239 = 655. 7 rows×84+48 = 636 ✓.\n\nBut wait — 02 list must also fit the thumb variant row (64 thumb inside 84 row → row2 content 64 high → row = 12+20+4+64+12 = 112). Rows: 6×84 + 112 + 48 = 664 > 655. Slightly over → reduce gaps to 6 (36): 652 ✓ or preview trunc... row2 thumb 60: 108. 6×84+108+36 = 648 ✓ ends at 239+648=887 ✓.\n\nAlright. Also `Header / Chat` (05, 06): V w 428 pad 8/24 gap 10:\n  r1: H FILL: IC menu 22; spacer; IC export 22. h 24\n  r2: H gap 10: IMG logo 36; V gap 1: T(\"Chat Bot AI 4.5\", BR SemiBold 18); H gap 4: PremiumBadge (small) — badge maybe: T(\"Premium account\", NU SemiBold 11.5 primary) + IC premium 12 primary (no bg pill to save space? use tint pill). h ~40.\n  Height ≈ 8+24+10+40 = 82 → messages start y=47+82+12=141.\n\nComponent positioning on page: components zone starting y=3400. I'll append each component node and set x/y.\n\nAlso creating component nodes: figma.createComponent(); c.resizeWithoutConstraints; add children. For components with auto layout, createComponent then set layoutMode etc. My helpers F/V/H create frames; for components I'll write C_V/C_H variants using createComponent. Simpler: build frame with helpers, then `figma.createComponentFromNode(frame)` — converts to component preserving everything. Yes! createComponentFromNode exists. Use it.\n\nVariant sets: combineAsVariants(nodes, parent) then set name; variant naming: each node name must be \"Prop=Value\". So name them \"View=Chats\" etc BEFORE combining.\n\nNote on strokes for cards: f.strokes=[S(HEX.border)]; f.strokeWeight=1.\n\nAlso for text FILL inside V/H stacks: after appendChild, set child.layoutSizingHorizontal=\"FILL\" (works if parent AL and child not absolute). For texts also set textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\" before FILL? FILL sets width; with textTruncation ENDING + maxLines it will ellipsize. lineHeight set.\n\nDivider helper: rect(w,1,0,S(border)).\n\nOK — Call 2 code (components). It's long but manageable. Let me also number: I'll store created component IDs and return them for later calls:\n\nReturn {viewSw:{chats,id...}, chatItem:{def,thumb}, exportRow, imageTile, suggestion, settingsRow, bubbleU, bubbleAI, msgActions, badge, homeHeader, chatHeader, newTopicPill?...}\n\nFor instances later: figma.createComponentInstanceById? No — need component node: await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id).createInstance(). Fine, I return IDs.\n\nImportant: variants combined — instances created from the SET's variants: getNodeByIdAsync(variantNodeId).createInstance().\n\nLet me now write Call 2.\n\nAlso remember: newTopic pill is part of HomeHeader (nested in component). Nested components-in-components: I'm building HomeHeader as plain frame with pill as plain frame (not component) — simpler; pill built by helper function in each call. Fine.\n\nAlso I realize for the chat list rows I need instance text overrides: question/preview/time. Instance children accessible via inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"question\"). After setProperties? These texts are NOT bound to component properties, so direct characters edit on instance children is allowed (override). Yes.\n\nTime values: \"28 mins ago\",\"3 days ago\",\"12 days ago\",\"16 days ago\",\"17 days ago\",\"20 days ago\",\"2 months ago\".\n\nData for chat rows (question / preview):\n1. q \"How can I forget a bad memory?\" p \"Forgetting a bad memory entirely may be challenging, as memories are complex and deeply ingrained in the brain. However, there are strategies you can use to cope with and reduce the impact of negative memories.\" t \"28 mins ago\"\n2. q \"Tell me the story of a student who was going to school and some interesting things happened to her on the way.\" p \"I'll try to create that. Here is the image I generated based on your description. I hope you like it. 😊\" t \"3 days ago\" + image\n3. q \"What can I do to increase concentration while studying?\" p \"Improving concentration while studying involves adopting effective study habits, creating a conducive environment, and taking care of your overall well-being.\" t \"12 days ago\"\n4. q \"What do you know about the French Revolution?\" p \"The French Revolution was a period of radical social and political change in France that lasted from 1789 to 1799.\" t \"16 days ago\"\n5. q \"Who is Pope Francis?\" p \"As of my last knowledge update in January 2022, Pope Francis, born Jorge Mario Bergoglio, is the head of the Roman Catholic Church.\" t \"17 days ago\"\n6. q \"How to get more followers on Instagram?\" p \"Increasing your followers on Instagram requires a combination of strategies to engage with your audience and attract new followers.\" t \"20 days ago\"\n7. q \"Tell me about the latest trends in fashion design\" p \"As of my last knowledge update in January 2022, I can provide some general trends that were prevalent in fashion design.\" t \"2 months ago\"\n\nOK, write Call 2 now. I'll try to keep code under ~9k chars.\n\nOne risk: `inst.rescale()` — rescale exists on LayoutMixin (yes: rescale(scale: number)). ok.\n\nAnother: text truncation maxLines requires textTruncation=\"ENDING\" set first. OK.\n\nAlso for strokes on instances (Text Field filled state): override stroke color on instance root: i.strokes=[S(HEX.primary)]. Allowed (override).\n\nLet me write it.\n\n```js\nconst PAGE = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"5:2\");\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(PAGE);\nconst BR=s=>({family:\"Bricolage Grotesque\",style:s}), NU=s=>({family:\"Nunito\",style:s});\nfor (const s of [\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\"]) await figma.loadFontAsync(BR(s));\nfor (const s of [\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\",\"ExtraBold\"]) await figma.loadFontAsync(NU(s));\nconst HEX={primary:\"612A74\",dark:\"4A2160\",tint:\"F5EEF8\",bg:\"F7F5F9\",surface:\"FFFFFF\",text:\"211A2B\",sub:\"6B6176\",faint:\"A79DB2\",border:\"E7E2EC\",field:\"F2EEF5\",danger:\"D93843\",warn:\"C77700\",stImg:\"9E5FC1\",stExp:\"D9C1E8\",stFree:\"ECE6F0\"};\nconst hx=h=>({r:parseInt(h.slice(0,2),16)/255,g:parseInt(h.slice(2,4),16)/255,b:parseInt(h.slice(4,6),16)/255});\nconst S=(h,o)=>{const p={type:\"SOLID\",color:hx(h)};if(o!=null)p.opacity=o;return p;};\nfunction T(chars,font,size,color,o={}){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName=font;t.fontSize=size;t.charac