{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a full product design in an assigned Figma file for a benchmark (unattended session). Requirements:\n   - File: https://www.figma.com/design/S5iN4noHDacG8jTW5ILkwU/ (fileKey S5iN4noHDacG8jTW5ILkwU). Use ONLY this file.\n   - Verified account must be zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (confirmed via whoami ✓).\n   - Read 00 · Start Here for product/screens/states/data/copy/prototype requirements; 01 · Foundations for visual rules; reuse 02 · Components; reuse 04 · Media assets. Preserve all reference pages and their nodes.\n   - Deliver the complete design inside 03 · Workspace (page exists, currently EMPTY — confirmed). New frames, reusable components, and prototype connections allowed there.\n   - Build exactly 12 frames with exact names, wire as clickable prototype with listed links.\n   - Use Figma tools directly (whoami → get_metadata → read-only use_figma → use_figma build → get_screenshot verify). No delegation.\n   - Before EVERY tool call: a concise visible decision summary prefixed exactly \"Reasoning summary:\" in the same assistant message. After each tool result, same before next call. Final response: \"Reasoning summary: ...\" first line, then \"Final answer:\" and the answer.\n   - Finish by reporting: file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations.\n\n   THE PRODUCT (from 00 · Start Here): \"Chat Bot AI — AI assistant app\". Design complete mobile app: Sam Rivera logs in, browses past chats, generated images and PDF exports, starts a new chat, continues a conversation ending with a generated image, exports it as PDF, manages profile/theme/cloud storage. Canvas 428 × 928, light mode only. Home/conversation/Cloud Space may scroll vertically. Today = Dec 30, 2023. Must-include lists are grouped by subject, sorted A–Z; layout/styling are designer's choice. Copy/data must match \"Fixed data\" exactly. Long answers may cut off at frame end but everything listed must be visible. Brief wins over knowledge of the original kit. Do not add frames beyond the 12.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via use_figma tool (code ≤50,000 chars per call, each call an independent sandbox — no shared state between calls; must re-load fonts and re-fetch nodes each call)\n   - `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)` required to switch pages; `figma.getNodeByIdAsync` for node access\n   - Component instances: `component.createInstance()`, property override via `instance.setProperties({\"Label#3:0\": \"...\"}\")`, child overrides (fills, characters)\n   - `node.rescale(scale)` to size icon instances; recolor by setting fills/strokes on vector children\n   - Image fills: `{type:\"IMAGE\", scaleMode:\"FILL\", imageHash}` — hashes reusable in rectangles for cropped tiles\n   - Prototype wiring: `node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:\"CLICK\"}, action:{type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"}}]` (writable in plugin API — planned, wrap in try/catch to verify)\n   - Sheets/dialogs: clone fully-built parent frame into overlay frame, add dim rect (black ~45%), add sheet/dialog on top; hotspot on dim for tap-outside\n   - Text: `textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\"`, `textTruncation=\"ENDING\"`, `maxLines`, lineHeight in PIXELS\n   - Fonts: load before text creation with `figma.loadFontAsync({family, style})`\n   - MCP rate limiting: intermittent \"tool call limit\" errors — retrying the same call works\n   - Auto layout frames (layoutMode VERTICAL/HORIZONTAL, paddings, itemSpacing, primaryAxisSizingMode/counterAxisSizingMode, counterAxisAlignItems \"CENTER\")\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - FILE PAGES: 0:1 \"00 · Start Here 设计任务\", 1:2 \"01 · Foundations 视觉规范”, 1:3 \"02 · Components 组件库”, 1:4 \"04 · Media 素材库”, 5:2 \"03 · Workspace\" (EMPTY — wsChildren: [])\n   - 01 · FOUNDATIONS (all read): Brand primary #612A74 (fixed); typefaces fixed: Bricolage Grotesque + Nunito; canvas 428×928 iPhone, light mode only. Everything else (neutrals, text colors, surfaces, semantic colors, storage-breakdown colors, type scale, spacing, radii, elevation) is mine to define consistently.\n   - 02 · COMPONENTS (read):\n     - Button (3:24): COMPONENT 380×56, fill #612A74, cornerRadius 36, child text \"Login\" Nunito:SemiBold 17 white. Component property: `{\"Label#3:0\":{\"type\":\"TEXT\",\"defaultValue\":\"Login\"}}`\n     - Text Field (3:29): COMPONENT 380×56, white fill, stroke #D9D4CF 1px, radius 16, child text \"Email\" Nunito:Regular 16 color #787069. Property: `{\"Placeholder#3:1\":{\"type\":\"TEXT\",\"defaultValue\":\"Email\"}}`\n     - Status Bar (3:34): COMPONENT 428×47, WHITE fill, black content (Inter Semi Bold 17 \"9:41\", signal bars, wifi, battery)\n     - Home Indicator (3:45): COMPONENT 428×34, WHITE fill, black 134×5 rounded bar\n   - 04 · MEDIA (read) — node IDs and data:\n     - Logo 4:8 (96×96, IMAGE fill hash `f8f9b5b3858b794701361638e2a43a34013ec18c`)\n     - Avatar_Neutral 4:11 (96×96, vector gray person, cornerRadius 48 — instance directly)\n     - Gen_Mug 4:19 (200×200, hash `b33e106bff3f641b1402654e9d9d5ffdf2a99637`)\n     - Gen_Rat 4:22 (133×200, hash `69eb0235ba6c4ae0e2fade7e7cf9ee08b2857f0f`)\n     - Gen_Statue 4:25 (300×200, hash `d6fed4696134f62100e5e107b55526d302491cde`)\n     - Gen_Student 4:28 (281×200, hash `13287f16160feaa047f4e410175f8eea38c72198`)\n     - PDF_File_Icon 4:31 (64×64, IMAGE hash `ec7a1e4bdcb78b49dae4e3467913fb50db21088a`)\n     - Logo_Google 4:42 (48×48, multicolor vector fills — DO NOT recolor), Logo_Facebook 4:48 (48×48)\n     - Icon components (stroke-based vectors, stroke color ~#0A0A0A, strokeWeight 3–4; component sizes: 48×48 for Plus/Search/Chats/Archive/Image/Document_PDF/Back/Arrow_Up_Right/Send/Menu/Export/Close/More/Delete; 56×56 for Email/Password/Show; 32×32 for Edit/Copy/Share/Regenerate/Download/Premium):\n       4:58 Icon_Email, 4:64 Icon_Password, 4:70 Icon_Show, 4:76 Icon_Plus, 4:82 Icon_Search, 4:87 Icon_Chats, 4:94 Icon_Archive, 4:101 Icon_Image, 4:110 Icon_Document_PDF, 4:116 Icon_Back, 4:121 Icon_Arrow_Up_Right, 4:128 Icon_Edit, 4:134 Icon_Copy, 4:139 Icon_Share, 4:145 Icon_Regenerate, 4:152 Icon_Download, 4:157 Icon_Send, 4:164 Icon_Menu, 4:171 Icon_Export, 4:177 Icon_Close, 4:182 Icon_Premium, 4:189 Icon_More, 4:197 Icon_Delete\n     - Story_Text 4:203 (2480 chars). Opening to use (truncated display): \"Once upon a time, in the quaint town of Meadowville, there lived a spirited high school student named Lily. Lily was known for her enthusiasm for learning and her adventurous spirit. One crisp autumn morning, as she set out for school, little did she know that this ordinary day would turn into an extraordinary adventure.\" (+ more paragraphs available if needed)\n   - FONTS AVAILABLE (confirmed): Bricolage Grotesque: Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold, ExtraBold (+Light/ExtraLight/96pt ExtraBold); Nunito: Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold, ExtraBold, Black (+italics)\n\n   - FIXED DATA & COPY (must use VERBATIM):\n     - User: Sam Rivera · sam.rivera@example.com · premium account · 278 days left · avatar = Avatar_Neutral · Theme: System default · Data & storage 83% Used\n     - Chats newest-first (question — answer preview — time):\n       1. \"How can I forget a bad memory?\" — \"Forgetting a bad memory entirely may be challenging, as memories are complex and deeply ingrained in the brain. However, there are strategies you can use to cope with and reduce the impact of negative memories.\" — 28 mins ago\n       2. \"Tell me the story of a student who was going to school and some interesting things happened to her on the way.\" — \"I'll try to create that. Here is the image I generated based on your description. I hope you like it. 😊\" + Gen_Student image — 3 days ago\n       3. \"What can I do to increase concentration while studying?\" — \"Improving concentration while studying involves adopting effective study habits, creating a conducive environment, and taking care of your overall well-being.\" — 12 days ago\n       4. \"What do you know about the French Revolution?\" — \"The French Revolution was a period of radical social and political change in France that lasted from 1789 to 1799.\" — 16 days ago\n       5. \"Who is Pope Francis?\" — \"As of my last knowledge update in January 2022, Pope Francis, born Jorge Mario Bergoglio, is the head of the Roman Catholic Church.\" — 17 days ago\n       6. \"How to get more followers on Instagram?\" — \"Increasing your followers on Instagram requires a combination of strategies to engage with your audience and attract new followers.\" — 20 days ago\n       7. \"Tell me about the latest trends in fashion design\" — \"As of my last knowledge update in January 2022, I can provide some general trends that were prevalent in fashion design.\" — 2 months ago\n     - Images (8, this order): Gen_Mug · Gen_Rat · Gen_Statue · Gen_Student · Gen_Statue · Gen_Mug · Gen_Rat · Gen_Student\n     - Exports (7, newest first: title · date · size): \"How can I forget a bad memory? · DEC 30, 2023 · 2.16 MB\" / \"How to get more followers on Instagram? · DEC 16, 2023 · 158 KB\" / \"Pope Francis · DEC 05, 2023 · 4.62 MB\" / \"The effects of morning exercise on the body · NOV 04, 2023 · 75 KB\" / \"New methods of advertising in Instagram · SEP 24, 2023 · 492 KB\" / \"Saffron export business · SEP 08, 2023 · 169 KB\" / \"The best cologne brands · AUG 16, 2023 · 27 KB\"\n     - New chat suggestions (title — detail): \"Brainstorm names — for my fantasy football team with a frog theme\" / \"Suggest some codenames — for a project introducing flexible work arrangements\" / \"Write a SQL query — that adds a “statu