{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a full product design in an assigned Figma file for a benchmark (unattended session):\n   - File: https://www.figma.com/design/S5iN4noHDacG8jTW5ILkwU/ (fileKey S5iN4noHDacG8jTW5ILkwU). Use ONLY this file. Account verified via whoami: zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (done in earlier session).\n   - Build complete design inside page 5:2 \"03 · Workspace\". Preserve all reference pages (0:1 \"00 · Start Here\", 1:2 \"01 · Foundations\", 1:3 \"02 · Components\", 1:4 \"04 · Media\") and their nodes. Do not create other files or switch accounts/teams. Use supplied Figma tools directly without delegating.\n   - Product: \"Chat Bot AI — AI assistant app\". 12 frames with EXACT names: 01_Login, 02_Home_Chats, 03_Home_Images, 04_Home_Exports, 05_Chat_New, 06_Chat_Conversation, 07_Export_PDF_Sheet, 08_Profile_Settings, 09_Account_Actions_Sheet, 10_Theme_Sheet, 11_Cloud_Space, 12_Clear_Cache_Dialog. Canvas 428×928, light mode only. No frames beyond the 12.\n   - Fonts: Bricolage Grotesque (titles/display) + Nunito (body). Brand primary #612A74. Reuse components from 02 · Components and media from 04 · Media.\n   - Prototype: wire listed links with CLICK → NAVIGATE reactions (all 30 already applied and verified in earlier session).\n   - PROCESS RULE (critical, verbatim): Before EVERY tool call include a concise visible decision summary prefixed exactly \"Reasoning summary:\" in the same assistant message; after each tool result too. Final response: \"Reasoning summary: ...\" on first line, then \"Final answer:\" and the answer. Inspect screenshots of all 12 screens, fix visible problems, re-verify. Finish with: assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations. Do not claim completion for unfinished work.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma (each call = independent sandbox; must re-load fonts and re-fetch nodes every call)\n   - **FILL-in-hug-parent collapse rule**: layoutSizingHorizontal=\"FILL\" on a child inside a HUG-width (primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\") auto-layout parent collapses the child to its min width (10px). Parent must be FIXED width for FILL to resolve.\n   - **textAutoResize refresh trick**: when FILL doesn't take effect on a TEXT node, re-setting textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\" (even if already set) forces layout recalculation.\n   - Setting textTruncation/maxLines/characters requires fonts loaded first (loadFontAsync for every family/style present).\n   - **resize() on auto-layout frames forces both sizing modes to FIXED** (the original bug that collapsed many frames) — repair: resize FIRST then set sizing modes, or set sizing modes after.\n   - Rate-limit pattern: \"You've reached the Figma MCP tool call limit for your Full seat on the Enterprise plan\" — simply retry the identical call; succeeds on 1st–2nd retry.\n   - get_screenshot with enableBase64Response=true returns inline image (needed to visually verify; URL-only responses can't be viewed).\n   - Instance ↔ component propagation: component-level layout/size fixes propagate to all instances (confirmed for Settings Row, Chat Item); instance trees can be traversed read-only (children visible with overrides).\n   - Stale-clone problem: overlay frames (07/09/10/12) were built as clones of base frames at build time; if the base is later repaired, the overlay's static/structural copy is stale. Clones containing instances update automatically; frames needing structural re-layout must be re-cloned manually (done for 07).\n   - Auto-layout parents manage child x/y — setting child positions inside auto-layout is ignored.\n   - Prototype reactions (verified earlier): `node.reactions=[{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"},actions:[{type:\"NODE\",destinationId:\"<id>\",navigation:\"NAVIGATE\",transition:{type:\"SMART_ANIMATE\",duration:0.3,easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}}}]}]` — all 30 wires applied.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - FILE: S5iN4noHDacG8jTW5ILkwU. Pages: 0:1, 1:2, 1:3, 1:4, 5:2 (build target \"03 · Workspace\").\n   - FRAME IDS (all 12 exist): 01_Login=13:23, 02_Home_Chats=13:70, 03_Home_Images=13:155, 04_Home_Exports=13:210, 05_Chat_New=15:226, 06_Chat_Conversation=15:284, 07_Export_PDF_Sheet=21:330, 08_Profile_Settings=21:411, 09_Account_Actions_Sheet=22:444, 10_Theme_Sheet=22:481, 11_Cloud_Space=24:587, 12_Clear_Cache_Dialog=24:695. Layout: rows at y0 (01–04), y1028 (05–07), y2056 (08–12); x = 0/508/1016/1524(/2032).\n   - WORKSPACE COMPONENTS: ViewSwitcher set=12:32 (variants 12:11/12:21/12:31, now h:42, tabs py=8); Chat Item set=12:47 (variant children 12:38 \"Image=None\" and 12:46 \"Image=With\" — BOTH now fixed: r1 FILL+FIXED 350, question FILL 281 maxLines 1 ENDING, time HUG, preview FILL maxLines 2, r2 FILL); Export Row=12:53 (title FILL 302); Image Tile=12:54; Suggestion Card=12:58; Settings Row=21:319 (main H FILL 380x40 CENTER gap12, labels V FILL 326 gap2, label/value texts FILL, note FILL); Bubble/User=12:74; Bubble/AI=12:77; Premium Badge=12:82; Header Home=12:106 (h:145, title FILL 336, r1 sp FILL, search text FILL, r3 c:AUTO); Header Chat=12:126 (id column c:AUTO 127 wide).\n   - 13:70 (02) chatlist: converted to VERTICAL auto-layout, itemSpacing=4, resize(380,·), p:AUTO/c:FIXED, y=266, h=626, ends 892 < home indicator 894. Children: 7 Chat Item instances (1× \"With\" variant at index 1 named link/storyCard).\n   - 15:226 (05) fixed: greet (c:AUTO, CENTER, gap8 → h47), suggestions (rows p:FIXED/c:AUTO gap12, cards resized 184x106, rows y0/y118), inputbar (resize 380x48, FIXED/FIXED, gap12, inputfield FILL=3